  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  High pressure rebuilding today with warming temperatures and\n   light diurnal winds.\n\n-  Thunderstorm chances expand northward Tuesday and Wednesday.\n\nHigh pressure will rebuild across the Northern Rockies today\nbringing stable conditions and generally light winds. High\ntemperatures will be on the uptrend, topping out about 10 degrees\nabove seasonal norms by Tuesday and Wednesday. \n\nMonsoonal moisture will begin spreading northward for Tuesday,\nintroducing shower and thunderstorm chances primarily up toward\nthe I-90 corridor. By Wednesday, deeper monsoonal moisture will\nbegin to encompass most of the region increasing the chances and\ncoverage of showers and thunderstorms. A mix of rain-producing\nstorms will intermingle with mostly dry thunderstorms elevating \nthe risk for more lightning-caused fire starts. \n\nEnsemble guidance continues to show agreement on a Pacific\nNorthwest trough returning into the forecast by the end of this\ncoming week into next weekend. At this time, there aren't many \ndetails on exact impacts or timing, but we can expect moderating\ntemperatures, and an increase in winds over a couple days which\nmay lead to another window of elevated fire weather conditions\nlater this week.",
